   "title": "Korea hosts G20 global financial stability conference in Seoul",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/20261027/korea-hosts-g20-global-financial-stability-conference-in-seoul",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:37:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793090222.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Korea's finance ministry on Tuesday hosted a global conference bringing together experts to discuss financial stability and supply chains in the era of artificial intelligence (AI). The Ministry of Finance and Economy and the state-run Korea Development Institute co-hosted the G20 Global Financial Stability Conference 2026 in Seoul, an annual event first held in 2013 to discuss ways to address global financial challenges.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国财政部周二主办了一场全球会议，汇集专家讨论人工智能时代的金融稳定与供应链。经济财政部和国有韩国开发研究院共同在首尔举办了2026年G20全球金融稳定大会。这是始于2013年的年度活动，旨在讨论应对全球金融挑战的办法。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea's finance ministry on Tuesday hosted a global conference bringing together experts to discuss financial stability and supply chains in the era of artificial intelligence (AI). The Ministry of Finance and Economy and the state-run Korea Development Institute co-hosted the G20 Global Financial Stability Conference 2026 in Seoul, an annual event first held in 2013 to discuss ways to address global financial challenges. Around 300 financial experts from across the globe participated in this year's event, discussing ways to enhance the stability and resilience of the global economy and address risks and challenges arising from AI-driven innovation, according to the ministry. In his opening remarks, Second Vice Finance Minister Huh Chang stressed the spread of AI and the restructuring of supply chains could pose new threats to financial market stability. Huh called for preemptive measures to address AI-related risks and sufficient financial capacity to cope with future turbulence, alongside efforts to link financial safety nets with supply chain resilience. Laura Alfaro, chief economist at the Inter-American Development Bank, said during a presentation that global imbalances could increase financial market volatility, noting the need to consider both corporate ownership structures and global production systems. The finance ministry said Korea will build on the discussions at the forum to strengthen global cooperation within the Group of 20 (G20) framework and enhance the resilience of the international financial system",
