   "_dt": 1793090222.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "The Korean won edged down against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, as traders have kept a close watch on a Federal Reserve meeting this week. The won was quoted at 1,323.7 won per dollar at 3:30 p.m., down 0.6 won from the close of the previous stock trading session. At one point in morning trading, the won advanced to a high of 1,322.8 won per dollar, helped by stronger-than-expected economic growth in the third quarter.",
   "summary_zh": "周二，韩元兑美元小幅走低，交易员密切关注美联储本周召开的会议。下午3时30分，韩元报1美元兑1,323.7韩元，较上一股市交易日收盘时下跌0.6韩元。早盘交易中，受第三季度经济增长强于预期的推动，韩元一度升至1美元兑1,322.8韩元。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Korean won edged down against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, as traders have kept a close watch on a Federal Reserve meeting this week. The won was quoted at 1,323.7 won per dollar at 3:30 p.m., down 0.6 won from the close of the previous stock trading session. At one point in morning trading, the won advanced to a high of 1,322.8 won per dollar, helped by stronger-than-expected economic growth in the third quarter. The nation's economy grew 1 percent in the July-September period, thanks to semiconductor-led exports and investment. Foreign investors purchased a net 592.9 billion won ($447 million) worth of local shares during the latest regular stock trading session, with the benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index gaining 3.09 percent to close at 5,638.34",
