   "title": "Akwa Ibom bans bills, posters on road kerbs, public infrastructure",
   "url": "https://businessday.ng/news/article/akwa-ibom-bans-bills-posters-on-road-kerbs-public-infrastructure/",
   "domain": "businessday.ng",
   "source": "BusinessDay（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:01:46 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793012506.0,
   "ageDays": 0.92,
   "summary": "Listen to this article Share Akwa Ibom State Government has prohibited the pasting or display of bills, posters, banners and other advertising materials on road kerbs, medians, bridges, public buildings and other public infrastructure across the State. According to the notice, any person or organisation found violating the directive shall bear the cost of removing such materials and restoring affected public infrastructure, in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.",
   "summary_zh": "收听本文 分享 阿夸伊博姆州政府已禁止在全州道路路缘、隔离带、桥梁、公共建筑及其他公共基础设施上张贴或展示账单、海报、横幅及其他广告材料。通知称，任何被发现违反该指令的个人或组织，均须承担清除此类材料并修复受影响公共基础设施的费用，并遵守适用法律法规。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Listen to this article Share Akwa Ibom State Government has prohibited the pasting or display of bills, posters, banners and other advertising materials on road kerbs, medians, bridges, public buildings and other public infrastructure across the State. Aniekame Umana, Commissioner for Information, who disclosed this in a statement over the weekend, said that the ban takes immediate effect. According to the notice, any person or organisation found violating the directive shall bear the cost of removing such materials and restoring affected public infrastructure, in accordance with applicable laws and regulations. The notice directed all concerned to remove any such materials already placed in these locations without delay. He said that security agencies and relevant government authorities have been directed to monitor compliance and take appropriate enforcement action against offenders in accordance with the law. He also reiterated the administration’s commitment to maintaining a ‘clean, orderly and aesthetically pleasing environment ‘, urging all residents and organisations to protect public infrastructure from defacement",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "sec"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_businessday",
   "title_zh": "阿夸伊博姆州禁止在路缘和公共基础设施上张贴账单及海报",
   "body_zh": "收听本文分享。阿夸伊博姆州政府已禁止在全州道路路缘、隔离带、桥梁、公共建筑及其他公共基础设施上张贴或展示账单、海报、横幅及其他广告材料。州信息专员 Aniekame Umana 周末在一份声明中透露了这项禁令，并表示禁令立即生效。通知规定，任何被发现违反该指令的个人或组织，均须按照现行法律法规承担清除此类材料并修复受影响公共基础设施的费用。通知要求所有相关人员立即移除已经放置在这些地点的此类材料。他说，安全机构及相关政府当局已获指示监督执行情况，并依法对违规者采取适当执法行动。他还重申政府致力于维护“整洁、有序且美观的環境”，敦促所有居民和组织保护公共基础设施，防止其遭到涂损",
